WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:17.340
Good morning, John. It's Tuesday, January
23rd. If you're wondering why I'm blowing

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:23.320
on my wine, it's because it's tea. But I needed
something that I could toast with. Congratulations

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:31.275
on your Printz nomination. That wasn't exciting
enough; I need to be more excited about that.

00:00:31.275 --> 00:00:37.080
To the Printz Award! To An Abundance of Katherines!
To Katherines! There's one sitting right here.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:45.100
She's waving. To silver medals! To not quite
doing as good as you did the last time!

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:47.289
Sorry, that was kinda mean.

00:00:47.289 --> 00:00:52.489
So I was in a bookstore today, and the lady
came up to me and said, "You're John Green's

00:00:52.489 --> 00:00:59.949
brother." Oh-ho! So it turns out I'm famous
now. Well, she might very well be your biggest

00:00:59.949 --> 00:01:05.089
fan. She has a section in her bookstore devoted
entirely to you. In fact, there are several

00:01:05.089 --> 00:01:09.950
sections in her book store devoted entirely
to you. Well they're all kind of small.

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:14.010
Uh, she had heard that you won the Printz
Prize. I don't know what you're gonna do with

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:17.500
all of them, man. You're just rackin' 'em
up. What do you do with two Printz Awards?

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:23.122
Do you actually get a thing? Do you get, like,
a statue? Ah congratulations! Or do you just,

00:01:23.122 --> 00:01:26.509
you know, every single one of your books get
a sticker on it. Which is cool. I like the

00:01:26.509 --> 00:01:29.280
sticker, I think the sticker is good. Or do
you just get more money? Do they give you

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:31.990
more money? Is there any, you know, reward?

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:36.090
Now there's something that I wanted to talk
to you about. When you received the information

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:40.950
that you were getting the Printz Award, one
of the things that you did not do was your

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:45.850
Happy Dance. Is your Happy Dance actually
your Happy Dance? Or are you just trying to

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:49.600
entertain us? Because if you're just trying
to entertain us, then this thing isn't real,

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:54.360
man, and it has to be real! Or you know, it
could be fake. We could start faking things,

00:01:54.360 --> 00:02:00.229
and that might be interesting. For example,
I generally sit by the fire, with a glass

00:02:00.229 --> 00:02:03.060
of wine... in my girlfriend's coat...

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:05.120
Katherine: Girlfriend?

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:14.000
Hank: Girlfriend, huuhhh... eheheh, yes...
girlfriend's coat. We aren't married 'cause

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:18.699
this is fake time. I'm lying about things.
Obviously.

00:02:18.699 --> 00:02:22.940
So I was recently at your friend Maureen Johnson's
blog. She discussed a long conversation which

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:30.190
you and Johnson and Lockhart had, concerning
the suffix, "in your pants." It turns out

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:36.480
that every book title becomes better when
you add "in your pants" to the end of the

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:41.760
title. I'm going to go around this lovely
cabin and find books.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:48.000
The Dance of the Dissident Daughter in Your
Pants! Present Moment, Wonderful Moment in

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:54.970
Your Pants. Stumbling on Happiness in Your
Pants. The Left Hand of Darkness in Your Pants.

00:02:54.970 --> 00:03:04.090
The Student Bible in Your Pants?

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:12.530
Yeah... So... I'll see you tomorrow.

00:03:12.530 --> 00:03:17.840
And I know that you don't personally know
this, but Katherines in your pants is actually

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:26.010
quite a nice thing. I don't know about an
abundance of Katherines... I promise, I don't.

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:31.369
But one Katherine in my pants... is quite
nice.

